BT /F1 10 Tf 12 TL 56 760 Td (Lunchbox Allergen Check) Tj T* () Tj T* (Executive Summary: Lunchbox Allergen Check) Tj T* () Tj T* (Problem) Tj T* () Tj T* (Food allergies affect a meaningful number of school-age children in the United States, and) Tj T* (parents of these children spend a great deal of time and energy making sure that what their) Tj T* (child eats is safe. Every school day involves decisions about lunch: whether to pack food from) Tj T* (home, whether the cafeteria menu is safe, and whether a snack that a friend or teacher offers) Tj T* (contains something dangerous. Ingredient labels can be long and confusing, and allergens often) Tj T* (appear under unfamiliar names. For example, milk may be listed as casein or whey, and wheat may) Tj T* (appear in ingredients that parents do not expect. Parents told us that reading labels is tiring) Tj T* (and that they worry they will miss something. Many also said that school menus are posted in) Tj T* (formats that make it hard to find ingredient information.) Tj T* () Tj T* (We believe this is a real source of anxiety for families and that a simple tool could make) Tj T* (daily routines easier.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Solution) Tj T* () Tj T* (Lunchbox Allergen Check is a phone app that lets parents scan a school lunch menu or the label) Tj T* (on a packaged snack and quickly see whether it contains their child's allergens. A parent) Tj T* (creates a profile for each child and selects the allergens that apply. When the parent points) Tj T* (the phone camera at a menu or label, the app reads the text and compares the ingredients) Tj T* (against the child's profile. The app then shows a clear result: safe, caution, or avoid. The) Tj T* (caution result is used when an ingredient is ambiguous or when a label includes a statement) Tj T* (that the product may have been made in a facility that handles an allergen.) Tj T* () Tj T* (The app is designed to be fast and easy to use, even for a parent who is in a hurry in a) Tj T* (grocery aisle or at the kitchen table in the morning. We also plan to let parents save results) Tj T* (so that they can look back at products they have already checked. In the future, we would like) Tj T* (to let parents share their child's profile with relatives, babysitters, and school staff.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Market) Tj T* () Tj T* (Our target customers are parents of school-age children with food allergies. A large number of) Tj T* (families in the United States have at least one child with a food allergy, and we believe this) Tj T* (represents a substantial market. Because the problem touches almost every school and every) Tj T* (community, we think the potential audience is broad. We also see secondary opportunities with) Tj T* (schools, summer camps, and after-school programs that want to help families manage allergies) Tj T* (more easily.) Tj T* () Tj T* (We have not yet conducted a formal market study. Our current understanding comes from) Tj T* (conversations with a small number of parents we know personally and from general reading about) Tj T* (food allergies. As part of our next steps, we plan to survey more families and to estimate the) Tj T* (number of likely paying users more carefully.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Business Model) Tj T* () Tj T* (We plan to use a freemium model. The free version would let a parent create one child profile) Tj T* (and run a limited number of scans each month. A paid subscription would unlock unlimited scans,) Tj T* (multiple child profiles, saved history, and sharing features. We are still deciding on the) Tj T* (price, but we are considering a monthly fee in the range of a few dollars, with a discount for) Tj T* (annual plans.) Tj T* () Tj T* (We also see possible additional revenue from partnerships with food brands that make allergy-) Tj T* (friendly products, and from licensing the app to schools. However, we have not discussed these) Tj T* (ideas with any potential partners, and we are not yet sure how they would work in practice. For) Tj T* (now, we expect subscriptions to be our main source of revenue. We have not built a detailed) Tj ET
endstream
