BT /F1 10 Tf 12 TL 56 760 Td (model of how many free users would convert to paid users, though we hope that a meaningful) Tj T* (share would find the app valuable enough to pay for.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Competition) Tj T* () Tj T* (There are other apps and websites that help people with food allergies, including barcode) Tj T* (scanners, ingredient lookup tools, and general nutrition apps. Many of these focus on adults or) Tj T* (on general dietary preferences rather than on children and school settings. We believe our app) Tj T* (will stand out because it is built specifically for parents of school-age children and because) Tj T* (it handles school lunch menus as well as packaged foods.) Tj T* () Tj T* (We recognize that existing apps may add similar features, and that a larger company could copy) Tj T* (our approach. Our advantage, we believe, will come from focusing on the needs of families and) Tj T* (from making the experience simple and trustworthy. We have not yet tested our app against) Tj T* (competing products, and we do not have a patent or other protection for our ideas.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Team) Tj T* () Tj T* (Priya Raghunathan is a junior studying computer science at our university. She will lead the) Tj T* (technical development of the app, including the scanning and text recognition features. Marcus) Tj T* (Delacroix-Whitfield is a senior studying business. He will lead marketing, partnerships, and) Tj T* (planning for the company. Tamsin Okonkwo is a junior studying public health. She will lead our) Tj T* (work on food allergy content, including how allergens are named and categorized, and will help) Tj T* (us speak with families and health professionals.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Each of us has a personal connection to the problem through friends or family members who) Tj T* (manage food allergies. We have formed Lunchbox Allergen Check as a limited liability company.) Tj T* (None of us has yet built or launched a consumer product, and we are learning as we go. We plan) Tj T* (to seek advice from faculty members and from mentors in the local startup community.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Milestones and Financials) Tj T* () Tj T* (We have not yet reached any formal milestones. We have formed the LLC and developed our) Tj T* (concept, and we have begun sketching how the app would look and work. We do not yet have a) Tj T* (working prototype, a website, or paying customers.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Over the next twelve months, we hope to build a first version of the app, test it with a group) Tj T* (of volunteer families, and use their feedback to improve it. We would then like to release the) Tj T* (app to the public and begin to grow our user base. We expect our main costs to be software) Tj T* (development, cloud services for text recognition, legal and insurance costs, and marketing. We) Tj T* (have not prepared detailed financial projections, but we estimate that we will need several) Tj T* (thousand dollars to build a first version and more as we grow. Revenue would begin only after) Tj T* (launch, and we cannot yet say when the company might break even.) Tj T* () Tj T* (What We Are Asking For) Tj T* () Tj T* (We are applying to this competition for several reasons. First, we would like funding to build) Tj T* (our first prototype and to pay for early costs such as legal fees and software tools. Second,) Tj T* (we would value feedback from the judges on our business plan, especially on pricing,) Tj T* (competition, and how to reach families. Third, we would welcome introductions to mentors who) Tj T* (have experience in consumer apps, food and health, or working with schools. Winning this) Tj T* (competition would help us move from an idea to a working product, and we are grateful for the) Tj T* (chance to present our plan.) Tj ET
endstream
